Let me update isSolid to include CRATE (solid). ONEWAY is solid only from top (falling). Let me handle oneway in verticalCollide: when falling (vy>0) and tile below is ONEWAY, land; but don't collide when moving up.

Let me update isSolid: add CRATE. Not ONEWAY (handled specially). 

Let me update verticalCollide to handle ONEWAY (land from top only), BOUNCY (super bounce), TRAMPOLINE (ultra bounce), CRATE (normal solid, and stomping breaks it - handle in interactions or collision). Crate break on stomp: when player lands on crate, remove the tile. Let me handle in checkTileInteractions or in verticalCollide.

Let me update verticalCollide:
```
function verticalCollide(obj, useSpring){
  ...
  for tx:
    var tb = tileAt(bottom row);
    if (obj.vy > 0 && (isSolid(tb) || tb===ONEWAY)) { land; if tb===BOUNCY -> vy=-19; if tb===TRAMPOLINE -> vy=-28; if tb===CRATE -> remove tile (grid) and maybe small; }
    else if (obj.vy<0 && isSolid(tt)) { head bump }
  ...
}
```
But verticalCollide is generic for enemies too. Let me keep it but add oneway/bouncy/tramp/crate only for player (useSpring param true). Let me pass useSpring true for player; for enemies false. Let me apply bouncy/tramp/crate/oneway only when useSpring (player). Enemies just use normal solid.

