parts.text:
The user wants pressing Space (to skip) during the boss/enemy intro should skip the WHOLE animation, not just the current phase/shot.

Currently, in the enemyintro state, pressing Space sets `introTimer = 0`, which advances to the next intro enemy (for multi-enemy levels) or starts the game. For boss cinematics (single boss), pressing Space sets introTimer=0, which advances introIndex++ → state='playing'. So for a single boss, pressing Space should skip the whole cinematic → playing. Let me verify.

Actually, let me look at the keydown handling. Currently:
```
if ((state === 'levelclear' || state === 'enemyintro') && (Space/Enter/N)) {
  if (state === 'enemyintro') { introTimer = 0; }
  else if (levelIndex < LEVELS.length - 1) loadLevel(levelIndex + 1);
  else state = 'victory';
}
```
So during enemyintro, pressing Space sets introTimer=0. Then in update(), enemyintro branch:
```
if (state === 'enemyintro') {
  if (!isFinite(introTimer)) introTimer = 0;
  if (introTimer > 0) introTimer--;
  if (introTimer <= 0) {
    introIndex++;
    if (introIndex < introEnemies.length) introTimer = introDuration(introIndex);
    else state = 'playing';
  }
  return;
}
```
So when introTimer=0 (set by Space), the next update: introTimer<=0 → introIndex++ → if introIndex < introEnemies.length, move to next enemy (for multi-enemy levels), else state='playing'.

For a single boss level, introEnemies=[{boss}], so introIndex++ → 1 → >=1 → state='playing'. So pressing Space skips the whole boss cinematic. Good — that should work.

But the user says pressing Space to skip should skip the whole animation. Maybe the issue is: for a boss cinematic, pressing Space sets introTimer=0, but the next update sets state='playing'. However, there might be a delay or the press needs to be held. Or maybe the issue is that pressing Space once doesn't fully skip — it advances to the next shot/enemy? 

Wait — for multi-enemy normal levels, pressing Space advances to the next enemy (not skip all). The user wants Space to skip the WHOLE animation (all enemies, straight to playing).

So the fix: pressing Space during enemyintro should set state='playing' directly (skip everything), not just advance one intro enemy.

Let me change the keydown handling: when state==='enemyintro' and Space pressed, set state='playing' (skip all intros) and introTimer=0.

Also, the menu navigation: the keydown has a menu block for state 'title'/'pause'/'gameover'/'victory', but 'enemyintro' isn't in that. And the levelclear/enemyintro block handles Space. Let me modify the enemyintro part to fully skip.

Let me change:
```
if ((state === 'levelclear' || state === 'enemyintro') && (Space/Enter/N)) {
  if (state === 'enemyintro') { introTimer = 0; state = 'playing'; }
  ...
}
```

This sets state='playing' directly, skipping all remaining intros.

But wait — there's also the canvas/menu handling. For enemyintro, Space should skip. Let me update.

Also, the ENEMY_INTRO for normal enemies — pressing Space should skip to playing. Yes.

Let me make this change. Also, ensure that when state='playing' is set, the game starts immediately (player already spawned).

Let me update the keydown handler.

Let me find the levelclear/enemyintro block and modify.

