```
This draws two vertical rails (at px+6 and px+TS-10) and rungs. The rails are 4px wide at x=6..10 and x=22..26. Rungs at y=py, py+8, ... width TS-10 = 22 (x=5..27). This looks OK but maybe the rails are too thin or the rungs overlap the rails. Let me improve the ladder to look like a proper ladder filling the tile: wider rails, centered rungs, maybe a subtle highlight, and a consistent size. Also, ladders often span multiple tiles — the visual should tile seamlessly (rungs continuous). Since each tile draws rungs at py, py+8, ... and rails, it tiles fine.

"right size" might mean the ladder doesn't fill the tile (too narrow) or the climbing collision box vs visual. Let me make the ladder clearly fill the 32px tile: rails at the sides (e.g., x=5 and x=23, 4px wide), rungs spanning between with even spacing (e.g., every 8px starting at py+4). Add a wood texture / highlight.

