parts.text:
The user says Level 25's boss animation is too similar to Level 5's — it needs to be an independent animation.

Level 5 boss = SLUDGE KING (skin 0). Level 25 boss = SWORD KNIGHT (skin 5).

The boss intro cinematics are handled by drawBossCinematic, which dispatches by skin:
- skin 4/rat → drawRatCinematic
- skin 1 → drawTarCinematic
- skin 2 → drawGolemCinematic
- skin 3 → drawGobblerCinematic
- else → drawSludgeCinematic

So skins 0 (SLUDGE KING, L5) AND skin 5 (SWORD KNIGHT, L25), 6,7,8,9 all use **drawSludgeCinematic** (the same shot-based cinematic). So Level 5 and Level 25 both show the same sludge cinematic (just with different boss bodies). That's why they look the same.

I need to create INDEPENDENT cinematic animations for skins 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 (sword knight, gunslinger, ghost, tank, laser bot), so each boss has its own unique intro.

I already made unique intro animations for skins 1 (tar), 2 (golem), 3 (gobbler), 4 (rat). But skins 5-9 all fall through to drawSludgeCinematic (the generic shot-based one). So L5 (sludge, skin 0) and L25 (knight, skin 5) share it.

The user specifically mentions Level 25 (SWORD KNIGHT) vs Level 5 (SLUDGE KING). I should give the SWORD KNIGHT (and ideally 6-9 too) their own unique cinematics.

Let me create unique cinematic animations for skins 5, 6, 7, 8, 9:
- SWORD KNIGHT (5): a knight cinematic — armor assembling, sword drawn, heroic march, cape.
- GUNSLINGER (6): western showdown — duel, guns drawn, muzzle flashes.
- GHOST WRAITH (7): ghost — rising from the floor, spectral, haunting.
- SPIKED TANK (8): tank — heavy rumble, spikes, approaching.
- LASER BOT (9): robot — powering up, laser charging, scanning.

