parts.text:
The current laser cinematic is the subtle power-up sequence. Let me replace it with a dramatic version: a big laser bot that strides in, hovers, spins its rotor (in body), scans, charges, and fires a huge beam. This will be clearly animated throughout.

Let me write a new dramatic drawLaserCinematic. I'll keep it full length but make it engaging.

New design:
- Dark backdrop with animated scrolling grid + floating energy particles.
- A BIG laser bot (scale ~2.2) that walks/slides in from the left to center with hover bob, rotor spinning (body), scanning eye.
- Boot text + progress.
- A dramatic laser charge building then a huge beam that fires across the whole screen at the end, with recoil.
- Name reveal.

Let me use boss.introTotal for phases. The intro is 2160 frames (~36s). I'll distribute:
- 0-0.5: robot strides in from left and settles (x moves), bobbing, rotor spinning, eye scanning, grid scrolling.
- 0.4-0.8: laser charges (glow grows, arcs, screen brightens), robot tilts back.
- 0.7-1.0: beam fires across screen, then name reveal + fade.

Let me write it with clear motion.

Let me define x = cx - 500 + ease(p/0.5)*500 (walks in over first half).

Let me write:
```
function drawLaserCinematic() {
  var total = boss.introTotal || 2400;
  var p = Math.min(1, (total - introTimer) / total);
  var cx = CANVAS_W/2, cy = CANVAS_H/2;
  // animated scrolling tech grid
  ctx.fillStyle = '#050a0e'; ctx.fillRect(0,0,CANVAS_W,CANVAS_H);
  var off = (p*total/4) % 32;
  ctx.strokeStyle='rgba(43,212,255,0.14)'; ctx.lineWidth=1;
  for(var gx=-off; gx<CANVAS_W; gx+=32){ ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(gx,0); ctx.lineTo(gx,CANVAS_H); ctx.stroke(); }
  for(var gy=0; gy<CANVAS_H; gy+=32){ ctx.beginPath(); ctx.moveTo(0,gy); ctx.lineTo(CANVAS_W,gy); ctx.stroke(); }
  // rising energy particles
  for(var ep=0; ep<24; ep++){ var ex=(ep*73)%CANVAS_W; var ey=CANVAS_H-((p*600+ep*41)%CANVAS_H); ctx.fillStyle='rgba(43,212,255,'+(0.15+Math.abs(Math.sin(p*8+ep))*0.3)+')'; ctx.fillRect(ex,ey,2,2); }
  // ground glow line
  ctx.fillStyle='rgba(43,212,255,0.15)'; ctx.fillRect(0, cy+92, CANVAS_W, 4);

  // big laser bot strides in from the left
  var inEase = Math.min(1, p/0.5);
  var bx = cx - 520 + inEase*520;
  var hover = Math.sin(p*20)*6;
  var tilt = Math.sin(p*20)*0.04;
  ctx.save(); ctx.translate(bx, cy+86 + hover); ctx.rotate(tilt); ctx.scale(2.2,2.2); drawBossBody(9,0,0,1); ctx.restore();

  // boot text with blinking cursor
  ctx.fillStyle='#2bd4ff'; ctx.font='bold 16px \"Courier New\", monospace'; ctx.textAlign='left';
  var steps=[['BOOT SEQUENCE...',0],['CALIBRATING OPTICS...',0.25],['CHARGING LASER...',0.5]];
  for(var si=0; si<steps.length; si++){ if(p>steps[si][1]){ ctx.fillStyle = si===2?'#ff6a2b':'#2bd4ff'; ctx.fillText(steps[si][0], 40, 60+si*22); } }
  ctx.textAlign='left';

  // laser charge
  var lg = Math.min(1,(p-0.55)/0.2);
  // charging eye glow + arcs on the robot eye (at its position)
  var ey = bx + 16*2.2, eyy = cy+86+hover-22*2.2;
